# Test-image requirements (lays markdown/markdown-table libs on the base image).
# NOTE — this is layered SEPARATELY from requirements.in on purpose: the README
# table validator (scripts/validate.py, tests/test_readme_tables.py) needs
# markdown-it-py + tabulate, but those are TEST-ONLY and must not leak into the
# production requirements.txt (baked into the ghcr image that the README is the
# source-of-truth for). One -c to the base pins so the full tree stays coherent.
#
# Makefile wiring — `make requirements-test` (docker):
#   docker run ... make _requirements-test
# Host equivalence — the SAME pip-compile the base uses, just with this file:
#   pip-compile --output-file requirements-test.txt requirements-test.in
-c requirements.txt
markdown-it-py>=4.0,<5
tabulate>=0.9,<1
